-- title:
--   The tail semigroups of resolvent maps
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. Let $K$ be closed and convex and $T$ nonexpansive, with resolvents $R_n$.
--
--   1. **Weak tail family.** For $m\in\mathbb N$, the weak selfmaps whose underlying maps lie in the convex hull of the tail family $\{R_n\circ g:\ n\ge m,\ g\text{ generated}\}$.
--   2. **Properties.** These families are nonempty for $m\ge1$, decreasing in $m$ and convex. They consist of generated nonexpansive maps and are closed under composition.
--   3. **Tail idempotent.** If the weak carrier is compact Hausdorff, there is a nonexpansive $P$ with
--   $$
--   P\circ P=P,\qquad P\in\bigcap_{n}\overline{\mathcal B_{n+1}} .
--   $$
